      "text": "you should not have feared man more than God, D&C 3:7 (30:1). Fear not to do good, D&C 6:33. whosoever belongeth to my church need not fear, D&C 10:55. not fearing what man can do, D&C 30:11 (122:9). fear not, for the kingdom is yours, D&C 38:15. if ye are prepared ye shall not fear, D&C 38:30. Fear not, little children, for you are mine, D&C 50:41. not open their mouths … because of the fear of man, D&C 60:2. let the rebellious fear and tremble, D&C 63:6. shall deny the faith and shall fear, D&C 63:16. there were fears in your hearts, D&C 67:3. strip yourselves from … fears, D&C 67:10. be of good cheer, and do not fear, D&C 68:6. fear not, let your hearts be comforted, D&C 98:1. fear not even unto death, D&C 101:36. fear not thine enemies, D&C 136:17.",
